SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Dormition eve\, Anogi
LOCATION:Anogi\, Ithaca\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 14 August the mountain hamlet of Anogi\, home to the byzantine church of the Dormition with its frescoes and Venetian bell tower\, hosts a panigiri in the church courtyard: the villagers roast meat and pour their own wine\, and there is dancing until sunrise. Ithacans call it the most fun night of the summer\; the drive from Stavros is short but winding\, so share a car.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ithaca/#anogi-panigiri-of-the-dormition-eve-anogi
